snp2.11:7.1 starts: Avoid the theme of beauty,
snp2.11:7.2 starts: connected with passion.
snp2.11:7.3 starts: Develop the mind in the unattractive—
snp2.11:7.4 starts: gathered into one, well-centered.
snp2.12:13.1 starts: Was the holy life, as led by Kappa
snp2.12:13.2 starts: in line with his aim? Was it not
snp2.12:13.3 starts: Did he unbind with no fuel remaining?
snp2.12:13.4 starts: Let us hear how he was released.”
snp2.13:7.1 starts: Having rightly found the Dhamma,
snp2.13:7.2 starts: he is unobstructed in speech, mind, & act.
snp2.13:7.3 starts: Aspiring to unbinding,
snp2.13:7.4 starts: he would wander rightly in the world.
snp2.14:8.1 starts: And these brahmans, debaters by habit,
snp2.14:8.2 starts: any elderly brahmans,
snp2.14:8.3 starts: and any others who consider themselves debaters,
snp2.14:8.4 starts: all depend on you for the meaning.
snp2.14:17.1 starts: Having heard the Dhamma taught by the One
snp2.14:17.2 starts: the disciple of foremost discernment, having considered it,
snp2.14:17.3 starts: should resort to almsfood, a dwelling, a place
snp2.14:17.4 starts: and water for washing dust from his robe.
snp2.14:18.1 starts: So a monk should stay unsmeared by these
snp2.14:18.2 starts: almsfood, a dwelling, a place to sit &
snp2.14:18.3 starts: and water for washing dust from his robe—
snp2.14:18.4 starts: like a water-drop on a lotus.
snp2.9:3.1 starts: should go at the proper time,
snp2.9:3.2 starts: humbly, casting off arrogance,
snp2.9:3.3 starts: should both recollect & follow
snp2.9:3.4 starts: the Dhamma, its meaning,
snp2.9:6.1 starts: Understanding’s the heartwood
snp2.9:6.2 starts: concentration, the heartwood
snp2.9:6.3 starts: When a person is hasty & heedless
snp2.9:6.4 starts: his discernment & learning
snp2.10:3.1 starts: Cross over the attachment
snp2.10:3.2 starts: remain, desiring,
snp2.10:3.3 starts: tied.
snp2.10:3.4 starts: Don’t let the moment pass by.
snp2.10:3.5 starts: Those for whom the moment is past
snp2.10:3.6 starts: grieve, consigned to hell.
snp2.11:1.1 starts: “From living with him often
snp2.11:1.2 starts: do you not despise the wise man?
snp2.11:1.3 starts: Is the one who holds up the torch
snp2.11:1.4 starts: honored by you?”
snp2.11:2.1 starts: “From living with him often
snp2.11:2.2 starts: I don’t despise the wise man.
snp2.11:2.3 starts: The one who holds up the torch
snp2.11:2.4 starts: is honored by me.”
snp2.12:5.1 starts: Cut through our uncertainty. Tell me this,
snp2.12:5.2 starts: make known, One of discernment deep,
snp2.12:5.3 starts: Like Thousand-eyed Sakka, in the midst of
snp2.12:5.4 starts: speak, All-around Eye, in ours.
snp2.12:10.1 starts: Pleading, I shall get the pure one
snp2.12:10.2 starts: he whose birth & death are abandoned.
snp2.12:10.3 starts: For people run-of-the-mill haven’t the power
snp2.12:10.4 starts: but Tathāgatas do have the power
snp2.14:19.1 starts: As for the householder protocol,
snp2.14:19.2 starts: one becomes a good disciple,
snp2.14:19.3 starts: since the entire monk-practice
snp2.14:19.4 starts: can’t be managed by those wealthy in
